--- !u!114 &1977586923
MonoBehaviour:
  m_ObjectHideFlags: 0
  m_CorrespondingSourceObject: {fileID: 0}
  m_PrefabInstance: {fileID: 0}
  m_PrefabAsset: {fileID: 0}
  m_GameObject: {fileID: 1977586921}
  m_Enabled: 1
  m_EditorHideFlags: 0
  m_Script: {fileID: 11500000, guid: c85a3a22ca7542140990d13250654bd5, type: 3}
  m_Name: 
  m_EditorClassIdentifier: Assembly-CSharp::UIPromptController
  pages:
  - pageName: Page 1
    pageText: Tap the apparatus required to perform this experiment.
    showDialogBox: 1
    showAlternatePanels: 0
    alternatePanels: []
  - pageName: Page 2
    pageText: Drag the white paper sheet and fix it on the drawing board using drawing
      pins.
    showDialogBox: 1
    showAlternatePanels: 0
    alternatePanels: []
  - pageName: Page 3
    pageText: Drag the ruler and place it in the middle of the paper.
    showDialogBox: 1
    showAlternatePanels: 0
    alternatePanels: []
  - pageName: Page 4
    pageText: Using the pencil draw a line which divides the paper into two halves.
      Ensure that the tip of the pencil is sharp.
    showDialogBox: 1
    showAlternatePanels: 0
    alternatePanels: []
  - pageName: Page 5
    pageText: Drag the pencil and mark a point at the center of the line. We shall
      call it O<sub>1</sub>.
    showDialogBox: 1
    showAlternatePanels: 0
    alternatePanels: []
  - pageName: Page 6
    pageText: Now, drag and place the prism such that its base aligns with line XY.
    showDialogBox: 1
    showAlternatePanels: 0
    alternatePanels: []
  - pageName: Page 7
    pageText: Draw the boundaries of the prism using the pencil and name its vertices
      as A, B, and C.
    showDialogBox: 1
    showAlternatePanels: 0
    alternatePanels: []
  - pageName: Page 8
    pageText: Draw the boundaries of the prism using the pencil and name its vertices
      as A, B, and C.
    showDialogBox: 1
    showAlternatePanels: 0
    alternatePanels: []
  - pageName: Page 9
    pageText: Drag the protractor and drop it on one side of the boundary AB, its
      centre coinciding with point O<sub>1</sub>.
    showDialogBox: 1
    showAlternatePanels: 0
    alternatePanels: []
  - pageName: Page 10
    pageText: "Drag the pencil and mark a point at 90\xB0."
    showDialogBox: 1
    showAlternatePanels: 0
    alternatePanels: []
  - pageName: Page 11
    pageText: Draw a line normal to line XY passing through point O<sub>1</sub>.
    showDialogBox: 1
    showAlternatePanels: 0
    alternatePanels: []
  - pageName: Page 12
    pageText: Mark a point at 35<sup>o</sup> with the normal, so as to make an angle
      of incidence.
    showDialogBox: 1
    showAlternatePanels: 0
    alternatePanels: []
  - pageName: Page 13
    pageText: Enter the angle of incidence in the observation table.
    showDialogBox: 1
    showAlternatePanels: 0
    alternatePanels: []
  - pageName: Page 14
    pageText: Using the scale and pencil, draw the incident ray.
    showDialogBox: 1
    showAlternatePanels: 0
    alternatePanels: []
  - pageName: Page 15
    pageText: Drag and place the prism back on boundary ABC.
    showDialogBox: 1
    showAlternatePanels: 0
    alternatePanels: []
  - pageName: Page 16
    pageText: Drag and fix pins P<sub>1</sub> and P<sub>2</sub> vertically on line
      L<sub>1</sub>O<sub>1</sub>.
    showDialogBox: 1
    showAlternatePanels: 0
    alternatePanels: []
  - pageName: Page 17
    pageText: View the images of pins P<sub>1</sub> and P<sub>2</sub> from the opposite
      face of the prism and make them collinear.
    showDialogBox: 1
    showAlternatePanels: 0
    alternatePanels: []
  - pageName: Page 18
    pageText: Fix pins P<sub>3</sub> and P<sub>4</sub> such that the feet of all
      four pins are in one straight line.
    showDialogBox: 1
    showAlternatePanels: 0
    alternatePanels: []
  - pageName: Page 19
    pageText: Watch the points carefully
    showDialogBox: 1
    showAlternatePanels: 0
    alternatePanels: []
  - pageName: Page 20
    pageText: Using the pencils, mark the positions of pins P<sub>3</sub>  and P<sub>4</sub>
      .
    showDialogBox: 1
    showAlternatePanels: 0
    alternatePanels: []
  - pageName: Page 21
    pageText: Draw an emergent ray joining the marked points P<sub>3</sub>  and P<sub>4</sub>
      .
    showDialogBox: 1
    showAlternatePanels: 0
    alternatePanels: []
  - pageName: Page 22
    pageText: Extend the incident ray in forward direction.
    showDialogBox: 1
    showAlternatePanels: 0
    alternatePanels: []
  - pageName: Page 23
    pageText: Extend the emergent ray in backward direction.
    showDialogBox: 1
    showAlternatePanels: 0
    alternatePanels: []
  - pageName: Page 24
    pageText: fdgthtevsadd
    showDialogBox: 1
    showAlternatePanels: 0
    alternatePanels: []
  - pageName: Page 25
    pageText: 
    showDialogBox: 0
    showAlternatePanels: 0
    alternatePanels: []
  - pageName: Page 26
    pageText: "Now measure the angle of deviation \u03B4 and enter the value in the
      observation table."
    showDialogBox: 1
    showAlternatePanels: 0
    alternatePanels: []
  - pageName: Page 27
    pageText: Click on "Reset" and repeat the experiment for some more angles of
      incidence.
    showDialogBox: 1
    showAlternatePanels: 0
    alternatePanels: []
  - pageName: Page 28
    pageText: Mark another point at 40<sup>o</sup> with the normal as the angle of
      incidence.
    showDialogBox: 1
    showAlternatePanels: 0
    alternatePanels: []
  - pageName: Page 29
    pageText: Enter the angle of incidence in the observation table.
    showDialogBox: 1
    showAlternatePanels: 0
    alternatePanels: []
  - pageName: Page 30
    pageText: Using the scale and pencil, draw the incident ray.
    showDialogBox: 1
    showAlternatePanels: 0
    alternatePanels: []
  - pageName: Page 31
    pageText: Drag and place the prism back on boundary ABC.
    showDialogBox: 1
    showAlternatePanels: 0
    alternatePanels: []
  - pageName: Page 32
    pageText: Drag and fix pins P<sub>1</sub> and P<sub>2</sub> vertically on line
      L1O1.
    showDialogBox: 1
    showAlternatePanels: 0
    alternatePanels: []
  - pageName: Page 33
    pageText: View the images of pins P<sub>1</sub>  and P<sub>2</sub>  from the
      opposite face of the prism and make them collinear.
    showDialogBox: 1
    showAlternatePanels: 0
    alternatePanels: []
  - pageName: Page 34
    pageText: Fix pins P<sub>3</sub> and P<sub>4</sub>  such that the feet of all
      four pins are in one straight line.
    showDialogBox: 1
    showAlternatePanels: 0
    alternatePanels: []
  - pageName: Page 35
    pageText: 
    showDialogBox: 1
    showAlternatePanels: 0
    alternatePanels: []
  - pageName: Page 36
    pageText: Using the pencil, mark the positions of pins P<sub>3</sub> and P<sub>4</sub>
      .
    showDialogBox: 1
    showAlternatePanels: 0
    alternatePanels: []
  - pageName: Page 37
    pageText: Draw an emergent ray joining the marked points P<sub>3</sub> and P<sub>4</sub>
      .
    showDialogBox: 1
    showAlternatePanels: 0
    alternatePanels: []
  - pageName: Page 38
    pageText: Extend the incident ray in forward direction.
    showDialogBox: 1
    showAlternatePanels: 0
    alternatePanels: []
  - pageName: Page 39
    pageText: Extend the emergent ray in backward direction.
    showDialogBox: 1
    showAlternatePanels: 0
    alternatePanels: []
  - pageName: Page 40
    pageText: Drag the protractor and place it on line L<sub>1</sub>O<sub>1</sub>
      such that its center lies on point Z.
    showDialogBox: 1
    showAlternatePanels: 0
    alternatePanels: []
  - pageName: Page 41
    pageText: "Now measure the angle of deviation \u03B4 and enter the value in the
      observation table."
    showDialogBox: 1
    showAlternatePanels: 0
    alternatePanels: []
  - pageName: Page 42
    pageText: Move Next page to repeat the experiment for some more angles of incidence.
    showDialogBox: 1
    showAlternatePanels: 0
    alternatePanels: []
  - pageName: Page 43
    pageText: Mark another point at 45<sup>o</sup>with the normal as the angle of
      incidence.
    showDialogBox: 1
    showAlternatePanels: 0
    alternatePanels: []
  - pageName: Page 44
    pageText: Enter the angle of incidence in the observation table.
    showDialogBox: 1
    showAlternatePanels: 0
    alternatePanels: []
  - pageName: Page 45
    pageText: Using the scale and pencil, draw the incident ray.
    showDialogBox: 1
    showAlternatePanels: 0
    alternatePanels: []
  - pageName: Page 46
    pageText: Drag and place the prism back on boundary ABC.
    showDialogBox: 1
    showAlternatePanels: 0
    alternatePanels: []
  - pageName: Page 47
    pageText: Drag and fix pins P<sub>1</sub> and P<sub>2</sub>  vertically on line
      L<sub>1</sub> O<sub>1</sub> .
    showDialogBox: 1
    showAlternatePanels: 0
    alternatePanels: []
  - pageName: Page 48
    pageText: View the images of pins P<sub>1</sub> and P<sub>2</sub>  from the opposite
      face of the prism and make them collinear.
    showDialogBox: 1
    showAlternatePanels: 0
    alternatePanels: []
  - pageName: Page 49
    pageText: Fix pins P<sub>3</sub>  and P<sub>4</sub> such that the feet of all
      four pins are in one straight line.
    showDialogBox: 1
    showAlternatePanels: 0
